.TH LIBTRUST 3 "" "0.1.6" "Peios Library Functions"
.SH NAME
libtrust \- trustd client and configuration API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <peios/trust.h>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The library exposes ABI 1 through libtrust.so.1.
The installed header defines the complete API, result views, and ownership rules.
Inputs are borrowed for a call. Results own their views until freed.
Copy views before releasing their result.
Mutable subscription handles require exclusive access.
.PP
Certificate helpers that need no daemon compute a fingerprint, convert
between DER and PEM, normalize and resolve fingerprints against a given
list, and return the default control security descriptor.
.SH ERRORS
Result errors are POSIX error numbers.
.BR peios_trust_result_failure ()
returns the kind of failure, one of the
.B PEIOS_TRUST_FAILURE_*
constants: NONE, OTHER, DENIED, NOT_FOUND, MALFORMED, NOT_A_CA, EXPIRED or
NO_CERTIFICATE. Both are stable. Diagnostic text is intended for people.
A positive timeout in milliseconds covers connection, sending, and receiving.
Operations are not replayed after uncertain I/O failures.
.SH LINKING
Use pkg-config with the trust module.
The safe Rust wrapper is the trust-client crate.
.SH SEE ALSO
trust(1), trustd(8)
